      },
      "subject": {
        "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
      },
      "valueString": "Rash began approximately 36 hours ago, starting on the trunk and spreading to the scalp, face, and proximal limbs. Described as small red spots progressing to vesicles, some now crusted. Examination showed multiple erythematous macules, papules, and 2–5 mm vesicles at various stages, including crusted lesions; some vesicles were umbilicated. Generalised, not dermatomal, with greatest density on the trunk."
    },
